---
import Docs from '../../../layouts/Docs.astro'
import DocTable from '../../../components/DocTable.astro'
import RecipeCard from '../../../components/RecipeCard.astro'

const usage = `shotlist [<name>…] [options]`

const report = `{
  "changed": 1,
  "total": 2,
  "drift": [{ "field": "chromium", "was": "141.0.0.0", "now": "139.0.0.0" }],
  "results": [
    {
      "name": "order-row",
      "status": "changed",
      "ratio": 0.0213,
      "shot": "screenshots/out/order-row.png",
      "against": "content/guide/images/order-row.png",
      "diff": "screenshots/out/diff/order-row.png"
    }
  ]
}`

const api = `import { check, loadConfig, loadLibrary, shoot, withNumbering } from 'shotlist'

const loaded = loadConfig()
const { paths, finders } = loaded.config
const library = loadLibrary({ ...paths, finders })

const recipe = withNumbering(library.recipes.get('order-row')!)
await shoot(recipe, library, loaded, { install: true })

const results = await check([recipe], library, loaded)`

const schema = `# yaml-language-server: $schema=../../node_modules/shotlist/dist/recipe.schema.json`
---

<Docs
  title="Command line reference"
  description="Every shotlist command, option, exit code and environment variable, and the shape of the JSON report."
>
  <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold">Command line</h1>

  <div class="mt-6">
    <RecipeCard code={usage} lang="bash" />
  </div>

  <p>
    With one or more names, shotlist takes those recipes. With no names and no options, it lists the
    recipes it found.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-14 text-2xl font-bold">Options</h2>

  <DocTable
    head={['Option', 'Effect']}
    rows={[
      ['<code>--all</code>', 'Take every recipe'],
      ['<code>--install</code>', "Copy each image to the recipe's install destination"],
      ['<code>--check</code>', 'Re-take and compare against the installed images'],
      ['<code>--diff</code>', 'With <code>--check</code>, write a three-panel diff image'],
      ['<code>--json</code>', 'With <code>--check</code>, write the report to stdout as JSON'],
      [
        '<code>--lint</code>',
        'Parse every config, recipe, macro and data file, report everything wrong, and stop',
      ],
      [
        '<code>--warnings</code>',
        'With <code>--lint</code>, also report what is legal but probably unmeant',
      ],
      [
        '<code>--keep-going</code>',
        'Carry on past a recipe that fails, and list them all at the end',
      ],
      ['<code>--init</code>', 'Write a starter configuration and recipe; never overwrites'],
      ['<code>--config &lt;file&gt;</code>', 'Use a specific configuration file'],
      ['<code>--login &lt;name&gt;</code>', 'Sign in and save the named session'],
      [
        '<code>--using &lt;macro&gt;</code>',
        'With <code>--login</code>, sign in by running a macro',
      ],
      ['<code>--untrusted</code>', 'Run with the restrictions listed below'],
      ['<code>--allow &lt;host&gt;</code>', 'Permit an extra host; repeatable'],
      ['<code>--allow-path &lt;dir&gt;</code>', 'Permit an extra directory; repeatable'],
      [
        '<code>--allow-env &lt;name&gt;</code>',
        "Permit a recipe to read this variable from the run's environment; repeatable",
      ],
      ['<code>--deny &lt;name&gt;</code>', 'Forbid a file or folder name; repeatable'],
      ['<code>--help</code>', 'Print the option list'],
      ['<code>--version</code>', 'Print the version'],
    ]}
  />

  <h2 class="mt-14 text-2xl font-bold">Exit codes</h2>

  <DocTable
    head={['Code', 'Meaning']}
    rows={[
      ['<code>0</code>', 'Every recipe succeeded; with <code>--check</code>, nothing changed'],
      ['<code>non-zero</code>', 'A recipe failed, or a checked screenshot changed'],
      [
        '<code>--lint</code>',
        'Non-zero when a file has an error; warnings alone leave it at <code>0</code>',
      ],
    ]}
  />

  <h2 class="mt-14 text-2xl font-bold">Environment variables</h2>

  <DocTable
    head={['Variable', 'Effect']}
    rows={[
      [
        '<code>SHOTLIST_ENV</code>',
        'Names a recipe may read, in addition to <code>--allow-env</code>',
      ],
      [
        '<code>SHOTLIST_ENV_DENY</code>',
        'Variable names no config key or flag may grant; globs allowed, subtracted last',
      ],
      ['<code>SHOTLIST_DENY</code>', 'Forbidden names, separated by commas or colons'],
      [
        '<code>SHOTLIST_UNTRUSTED</code>',
        'Set to <code>1</code> for the effect of <code>--untrusted</code>',
      ],
    ]}
  />

  <p>
    These are read from the process environment. shotlist does not load a <code>.env</code> file — that
    name is one it refuses to open — so anything kept there has to be in the environment before the command
    runs. See
    <a href="/docs/how-to/sign-in">Capture a page behind a sign-in</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-14 text-2xl font-bold">Check statuses</h2>

  <DocTable
    head={['Status', 'Meaning']}
    rows={[
      ['<code>same</code>', 'Within the configured threshold and tolerance'],
      ['<code>changed</code>', 'Outside them'],
      ['<code>new</code>', 'Nothing is committed at the destination'],
      ['<code>skipped</code>', 'The recipe installs nowhere, so there is nothing to compare'],
      ['<code>failed</code>', 'The recipe could not be taken'],
    ]}
  />

  <h2 id="json" class="mt-14 text-2xl font-bold">JSON report</h2>

  <p>Written by <code>--check --json</code>. Human-readable output moves to stderr.</p>

  <div class="mt-6">
    <RecipeCard code={report} lang="ts" file="report.json" />
  </div>

  <DocTable
    head={['Field', 'Type', 'Meaning']}
    rows={[
      ['<code>changed</code>', 'number', 'How many screenshots differ'],
      ['<code>total</code>', 'number', 'How many were compared'],
      ['<code>drift</code>', 'array', 'Differences between this machine and the recorded baseline'],
      ['<code>results[].name</code>', 'string', 'Recipe name'],
      ['<code>results[].status</code>', 'string', 'One of the statuses above'],
      ['<code>results[].ratio</code>', 'number', 'Fraction of pixels that differ'],
      ['<code>results[].shot</code>', 'string', 'Path to the image just taken'],
      ['<code>results[].against</code>', 'string', 'Path to the committed image'],
      ['<code>results[].diff</code>', 'string', 'Path to the diff image, with <code>--diff</code>'],
    ]}
  />

  <h2 class="mt-14 text-2xl font-bold">Baseline file</h2>

  <p>
    <code>--install</code> writes <code>shotlist.baseline.json</code> beside the configuration file, recording
    the shotlist, Playwright and Chromium versions and the platform that produced the images.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-14 text-2xl font-bold">Node.js API</h2>

  <p>The command line is a wrapper over exported functions.</p>

  <div class="mt-6">
    <RecipeCard code={api} lang="ts" />
  </div>

  <DocTable
    head={['Export', 'Purpose']}
    rows={[
      ['<code>loadConfig()</code>', 'Read and validate <code>shotlist.config.yaml</code>'],
      ['<code>loadLibrary()</code>', 'Read recipes, macros and data files'],
      ['<code>shoot()</code>', 'Take one recipe; pass <code>browser</code> to reuse one'],
      ['<code>check()</code>', 'Compare recipes against installed images'],
      ['<code>withNumbering()</code>', 'Expand <code>numbered</code> into callouts'],
      [
        '<code>parseConfig()</code>, <code>parseRecipe()</code>, <code>parseQuery()</code>',
        'Validate a parsed YAML document',
      ],
      ['<code>Macro</code>', 'The macro schema'],
    ]}
  />

  <h2 class="mt-14 text-2xl font-bold">JSON Schemas</h2>

  <DocTable
    head={['File', 'Describes']}
    rows={[
      ['<code>shotlist/dist/config.schema.json</code>', '<code>shotlist.config.yaml</code>'],
      ['<code>shotlist/dist/recipe.schema.json</code>', 'A recipe'],
      ['<code>shotlist/dist/macro.schema.json</code>', 'A macro'],
    ]}
  />

  <p>Reference one from a file for editor completion and inline validation:</p>

  <div class="mt-6">
    <RecipeCard code={schema} lang="bash" file="screenshots/recipes/order-row.yaml" />
  </div>

  <p>
    The config's schema was <code>dist/schema.json</code> before 0.4.0, which named one of three files
    "the schema". That file is still written and <code>shotlist/schema.json</code> still resolves to the
    config schema, so an existing YAML header or editor setting keeps working. Both go at 1.0.
  </p>
</Docs>
